只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Battle-tested multi-agent collaboration playbook for DeepSeek Harness: model-tier routing, spec discipline, git single-writer rule — as an installable skill. 多 agent 管线里运行 DSH 的实战协作规范","id":"gh:1334366968","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"hermes-dsh-collab","slug":"Cavan-Ou/hermes-dsh-collab","topics":["agent-harness","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","multi-agent","skill"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Battle-tested multi-agent collaboration playbook for DeepSeek Harness: model-tier routing, spec disc"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ipline, git single-writer rule — as an installable skill. 多 agent 管线里运行 DSH 的实战协作规范"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# hermes-dsh-collab"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Hook DeepSeek Harness into your Hermes pipeline: automated dispatch, execution, and verification —"},{"id":"p3s2","text":" with quality gates that don't trust self-reports.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> 简体中文版见 README.zh.md"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Your AI assistant can work all day. The question is whether you can walk away."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"This skill makes it safe to: Hermes writes the dispatch spec, DSH executes it, Hermes verifies it — "},{"id":"p6s2","text":"and you only step in when a quality gate actually fails. Distilled from a real 14-day pipeline (30 c"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"ommits, 7/7 stages shipped without rework)."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"**Dependencies:** DSH 0.1.x (headless profile) + any orchestrator agent (built and tested with Herme"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ependencies:** DSH 0.1.x (headless profile) + any orchestrator agent (built and tested with Hermes)."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Why this exists"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Hermes is your personal assistant. DSH is a capable executor. The gap is the **operating contract** "},{"id":"p9s2","text":"between them: what a good dispatch spec looks like, which model tier to use for which stage, who is "},{"id":"p9s3","text":"allowed to commit, and how verification actually happens."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Most pipelines skip that contract and pay for it in rework. Recent work (COPE) shows planner/executo"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"r separation works — but only when the executor's behavior is controlled. This skill encodes those c"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"ontrols, from a pipeline where they were tested:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"- **Model-tier routing** — Flash (`reasoning: max`) for routine stages and for looking at images (th"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"e main model is natively multimodal — no vision tier, no vision patch), Pro for multi-file refactors"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" and long synthesis (its channel is currently down upstream; the table says so instead of pretending"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" otherwise). When in doubt: try Flash once — rework means escalate.\n- **Spec 3 iron rules** — Plan f"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"irst · test first (TDD red→green) · scope declaration. A spec missing any of these is not shippable."},{"id":"p11s6","text":"\n- **Git single-writer** — only the orchestrator commits. The executor never touches git, so history"},{"id":"p11s7","text":" stays linear and auditable.\n- **Quality gates owned by the orchestrator** — full test suite + build"},{"id":"p11s8","text":" + diff-vs-scope audit + real browser walkthrough. Self-reports are not evidence.\n- **Write-back via"},{"id":"p11s9","text":" cwd** — `cd <project> && dsh --profile headless \"task\"` writes straight back. No /tmp mirrors, no p"},{"id":"p11s10","text":"atch handoffs.\n- **Pitfalls with receipts** — every entry is a real incident: patch config *replaces"},{"id":"p11s11","text":"* whole sections (not deep-merge), `read` chokes on binaries while `read_image` needs the model to d"},{"id":"p11s12","text":"eclare image input, stale backend processes invalidate green tests…"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Either way, the next DSH session loads it automatically (bundle registers a skill provider; the copy"},{"id":"p14s2","text":" is picked up by the skills scanner)."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Verify with three checks:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"1. A new session lists `hermes-dsh-collab` in its skills\n2. Say *\"write me a dispatch spec\"* — the s"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"kill triggers on the scenario\n3. Ask *\"can the executor git commit?\"* — it says **no**, and explains"},{"id":"p16s3","text":" why (single-writer rule)"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## What's inside"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Shaped like DeepSeek's own repo skills (see `.agents/skills` in deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness): guida"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"nce rather than a checklist · points at sources of truth instead of restating them · a dedicated \"Wh"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"at NOT to do\" section."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"> **Install forms:** both supported — bundle (`dsh plugin add`, official distribution path, verified"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" on DSH 0.1.0-rc.6) and direct copy to `$DSH_HOME/skills/` (lightweight, no build)."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Observed results"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| Result | Evidence |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| **Quality gates catch systemic errors automatically** | In one long-synthesis run (74 design docs,"},{"id":"p23s2","text":" ~600K tokens), verification surfaced **3 inverted negative-features** and a \"universe feature\" (hai"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"rline borders: 78–100% across all five style families) — mistakes that would take hours of manual re"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"view and would likely slip through |\n| Routine stages on Flash ship without rework | 3/3 stages — TD"},{"id":"p23s5","text":"D red→green, all gates green, real-browser walkthrough passed |\n| The skill changes behavior | Live "},{"id":"p23s6","text":"session: after loading, DSH refuses to commit and restates the single-writer rule with reasons |"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"**Where you (the human) step in:** only on the escalation chain — a quality gate fails, or the same "},{"id":"p24s2","text":"stage retries twice. Everything else runs unattended."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Documentation"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- `SKILL.md` — the judgment guide itself (read this first)\n- `REPORT.md` — build report: design deci"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"sions, self-test methodology (isolated `DSH_HOME` verification), open items"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"**Roadmap:** bundle packaging (`dsh plugin add` support) · per-workspace failure isolation · live ro"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"uting-table refresh from the observations card · English mirror of references"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"> **Portability note:** the skill's \"sources of truth\" point at workspace-specific paths (e.g. `~/.d"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"sh/profiles/headless/*.patch.yml`). The rules are portable — update the paths to match your workspac"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"/profiles/headless/*.patch.yml`). The rules are portable — update the paths to match your workspace."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Contributing"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"This skill is meant to grow from real use. Hit a pitfall not listed here? Open an issue with the inc"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"ident (symptom → root cause → fix). PRs welcome in Chinese or English."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"MIT"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"*Built by running a real pipeline, not by reading docs.*"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
